  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a contributor, I want every app test to wait on a condition, not on time, so that a slow simulator never turns a CI run red (the class of #467 and #514).\n\n### Scope\n\nThe Opus review of #517 (finding 5) lists suites that still spin or sleep:\n- `App/SwiftHFRTests/.../ContentLoaderTests.swift:12`: an unbounded `Task.yield` spin;\n- `PseudoListsSnapshotTests.swift:118`;\n- `ReplyComposerDraftTests.swift:99, 215` and `ReplyComposerSendTests.swift:133`: 100 ms sleeps.\n\nReplace each one with a signal (`CheckGate`, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Accounts/AccountTestSupport.swift`) and keep every assertion. A time limit stays only as a suite-level backstop against a hang (#366, #468, #517).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] No `Task.sleep` and no `yield` loop used to wait in `App/SwiftHFRTests` (grep listed in the PR).\n- [ ] App job green.\n\nRefs #514",
